            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nBeef on kimchi fried rice, fried banana were great. Rosti with chorizo not so. Lack of service staff and communication.\nDec 2019 • Family\nL'Usine has consistently been in the top ten for various magazine's list of cafes to visit in HCMC. Opening in Phu My Hung was a natural progression after conquering various hotspots in town and in another expat suburb. Many staying nearby were excited at their arrival, evident from the daily crowds during the usual peak hours, especially during weekend brunch timings -it will be almost impossible to get a table if you came during 10am on weekends without a reservation.\n\nService wise - found it odd they don't assign more staff during the peak hours. Hard to get any staff's attention during those hours, and you could tell staff were overwhelmed and couldn't handle much more. Appreciated young marcom team who gifted us vouchers, but apparently of an item no longer on the menu. Senior service staff were not aware and weren't trained adequately to be able to tell the differences in English. Also, it seems like service staff were trained to serve items to a table at the same time? On at least three separate occasions, we could see one of our dishes waiting on the counter, waiting at least 5 to 10 minutes for the second dish to be ready. By the time they served us both dishes together, the first dish turned cold and is a lot less appetizing.\n\nFood-wise - the taste and texture for most dishes we've ordered were good. The beef slices that came with the kimchi fried rice was very tender and flavourful. The fried bananas were fried perfectly - crispy panko outside, warm and moist on the inside. Brownies were moist with a surprise peanut butter filling. Might be good to add that as a note in case of peanut allergies. The seemingly fat juicy pork that came with the Com Tam was cold on arrival so it tasty clammy. The rosti dish was not good - the rosti was made up of completely mashed and mushy potatoes, which is just wrong. The four 1-mm thick slices of chorizo were completely hidden under the eggs. Our friend's lasagna tasted like they had used the frying oil one too many times. \n\nOverall loved the chills feels and above average quality cafe foods, but honestly hope they manage to work out the teething kinks.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 6, 2020\nL Concepts C\nDear Maryyeo,\n\nThank you for taking the time to write a review about L'Usine Phu My Hung. It's important for us to know where we can do better. Glad to know that you enjoyed your overall experience with us.\n\nOur sincere apologies we did not meet your expectations regards service and food. We will definitely pass your feedback to our team for improvements. \n\nOnce again, thank you very much for your visit at L'Usine Phu My Hung. Please do let us know when you will be back as we would like another chance to ensure your experience with us is perfect!\n\nSincerely,\n\nL'Usine Team\nRead more\nWritten January 10, 2020\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
